<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48591" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίη</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεᾱρία</span></b>  (v. infr.), 
			Boeot.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θιαωρία</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐφ.Ἀρχ</span>.<i><span class="en">
			1892.34
		</span></i>: ἡ:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sending of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωροί</span> or
			<i>state-ambassadors</i> to the oracles or games, or,
			collectively, <i>the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωροί</span>
			<i>themselves, embassy, mission</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρίαν ἀπάγειν εἰς Δῆλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					58b
				</span></i>
			: pl., opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατεῖαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				556c
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγειν τῷ Διὶ τῷ Νεμείῳ
				τὴν κοινὴν ὑπὲρ τῆς πόλεως θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.115
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				4.8.2
			</span></i>, Decr.Byz. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.91
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεᾱρία</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				28.19.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>office of</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρός</span>, <i>discharge of that
				office</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς Ὀλυμπίαζε
			θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.16
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				19.10
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>being a spectator at the theatre</i> or <i>games</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1491
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔτ᾽ ἐπὶ θεωρίαν πώποτε ἐκ τῆς
					πόλεως ἐξῆλθες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cri.</u>
					52b
				</span></i>
			; personified in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				523
			</span></i>,al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>viewing, beholding</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρίης
				εἵνεκεν ἐκδημεῖν</span> to go abroad <i>to see the
			world</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.30
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ θεωρίης πρόφασιν</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπέμπειν τινὰ κατ᾽ ἐμπορίαν καὶ κατὰ
					θεωρίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					17.4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				11.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.24
			</span></i>; <i>pilgrimage</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				1047
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the mind,
				<i>contemplation, consideration</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				38b
			</span></i>: pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῖαι θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				517d
			</span></i>: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντὸς μὲν χρόνου πάσης
				δὲ οὐσίας</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				486a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τῶν ἀρχῶν, ἡ τῶν ὅλων
			θ</span>., <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				2p.55U.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.288S.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ποιεῖσθαι περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					989b25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ περὶ φύσεως θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				1p.3U.
			</span></i>, etc.: pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς σαθρὰς αὐτοῦ
			θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
			</span></i> Lac.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Herc.</u>
				124.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>theory, speculation</i>, opp. practice, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.5.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ περὶ τὰ στρατόπεδα θ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				6.42.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ νυκτεριναὶ καὶ ἡμεριναὶ
			θ</span>. <i>theoretic reckoning</i> of night and day, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				9.14.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ μαθηματικὴ θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Rom.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>sight, spectacle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				802
			</span></i>, etc.; esp. <i>public spectacle at the theatre</i> or
				<i>games</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1005
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Hier.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τοῦ Διονύσου θ</span>. the
			Dionysia, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				650a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> Rhet.,
				<i>explanatory preface</i> to a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελέτη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Chor.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hermes</u>
				17.208
			</span></i>, etc.: so in Philos., <i>continuous exposition</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Olymp.
				<u>in Mete.</u>
				18.30
			</span></i>, al.</div>
